/// What a shim over an Erlang API needs from Erlang's conventions: an atom
/// made from text, and `Result`, the shape of Erlang's `{ok, V}` and
/// `{error, R}` once the shim's Erlang helper has rewritten them.
///
/// ## Examples
///
/// ```ernest
/// Erl.atom("ready")
/// // => ready
/// ```
///
/// ```ernest
/// Erl.Ok(1)
/// // => Ok(1)
/// ```
///
/// since 0.1.0

/// Erlang's `{ok, V}` and `{error, R}`, as a shim's Erlang helper rewrites
/// them into `{'Ok', V}` and `{'Error', R}` (report §8.4).
///
/// ### Examples
///
/// ```ernest
/// Erl.Error("closed")
/// // => Error("closed")
/// ```
export type Result(v, r) = Ok(v) | Error(r)

/// The Erlang atom of the text.
export foreign fn atom(text : String) -> Foreign = "erlang:binary_to_atom/1"
